@node ptable_library__unified_partition_table_library "ptable.library: unified partition-table library"
@{b}@{u}ptable.library: unified partition-table library@{uu}@{ub}

@{fg shine}ptable.library@{fg text} parses every partition scheme a removable card might
carry ( @{b}RDB@{ub} , @{b}MBR@{ub} , @{b}GPT@{ub} , and the partition-table-less @{b}flat@{ub} superfloppy,
a whole-disk FAT volume) and publishes the result into
@{fg shine}partition.resource@{fg text} . A device driver and a filesystem handler then share
that one parse instead of each carrying its own.

You never run it yourself; other components open it. This document
explains what it does, what you see when it works, and how its behaviour
is configured. The @{fg shine}lsptres@{fg text} tool (see @{"  __PAIRED_1__  " link "lsptres.guide/Main"} ) shows what it has discovered at
runtime. The library ships alongside its consumer @{fg shine}compactflash.device@{fg text} ,
or embedded in a Kickstart ROM for cold-boot autoboot (see the
amigaos-kickstart-builder
(https://github.com/pulchart/amigaos-kickstart-builder) repo).

----------------------------------------
@{"<< Prev" link Main}  @{"Contents" link Main}  @{"Next >>" link What_it_does}

@endnode

@node What_it_does "What it does"
@{b}What it does@{ub}

Two jobs, at two different times.

@{b}Cold-boot autoboot.@{ub} At Kickstart cold start, before DOS exists, the
@{fg shine}compactflash.autoboot@{fg text} module calls @{fg shine}BootScanPartitions@{fg text} . The library
scans the card, publishes every partition it finds into
@{fg shine}partition.resource@{fg text} , loads any filesystem handlers stored in the RDB
into @{fg shine}FileSystem.resource@{fg text} , and then registers the @{b}RDB@{ub} partitions: the
bootable ones with @{fg shine}AddBootNode@{fg text} so they appear in the Early Startup boot
menu, the rest with @{fg shine}AddDosNode@{fg text} . This is what lets you boot straight off
an RDB-partitioned card in the PCMCIA slot.

MBR, GPT and flat partitions are published but not registered at cold
boot: DOS does not exist yet, so their mount configuration cannot be
read. The DOS-time automount mounts them a moment later.

Registering a partition needs a handler for its filesystem already in
@{fg shine}FileSystem.resource@{fg text} . FAT partitions match any registered @{fg shine}FAT\x@{fg text} handler,
every other filesystem must match its DosType exactly. With no handler
the partition stays published but unmounted, listed by @{fg shine}lsptres@{fg text} as @{fg shine}P---@{fg text} .

@{b}DOS-time scan and automount.@{ub} When a card is inserted after the machine
is up, the consumer's mount worker (brought up by @{fg shine}compactflash.automount@{fg text}
) calls @{fg shine}ScanPartitions@{fg text} to publish the card's partitions, then
@{fg shine}MountPartitions@{fg text} to mount them. On removal it calls @{fg shine}UnmountPartitions@{fg text} or
@{fg shine}MarkAbsent@{fg text} , depending on the configured policy.

A rescan is a reconcile, not an append: every entry for that device and
unit is first marked not-present, each partition found refreshes its
existing slot in place (geometry, DosType, name) or gets a new one, and
entries that are gone are freed. An entry that is gone but still mounted
is marked invalid ( @{fg shine}I@{fg text} ) instead, which is what you see after a card
swap. @{fg shine}ScanPartitions@{fg text} returns only the number of entries it published for
the first time, so a rescan of an unchanged card returns 0.

In @{fg shine}compactflash.device@{fg text} automount is on by default; @{fg shine}AUTOMOUNT 0@{fg text} in
@{fg shine}cfd.prefs@{fg text} turns off the mount step only. The scan still runs and the
partitions are still published, so @{fg shine}lsptres@{fg text} lists them. Removal is never
gated by @{fg shine}AUTOMOUNT@{fg text} .

----------------------------------------
@{"<< Prev" link ptable_library__unified_partition_table_library}  @{"Contents" link Main}  @{"Next >>" link Flows}

@endnode

@node Flows "Flows"
@{b}Flows@{ub}

The four use cases, shown as the LVO calls each one drives. They all end
at @{fg shine}partition.resource@{fg text} , the shared registry.

@{b}Cold-boot autoboot.@{ub} The @{fg shine}compactflash.autoboot@{fg text} cold stub calls
@{fg shine}BootScanPartitions@{fg text} ; bootable RDB partitions become boot-menu entries,
the other RDB partitions mountable volumes. MBR, GPT and flat partitions
are published only.

@{fg highlight}
  +----------------------------+                                                
  |   compactflash.autoboot    |                                                
  +----------------------------+                                                
                 |                                                              
                 |                                                              
                 |                                                              
                 |                                                              
                 v                                                              
  +----------------------------+                                                
  |     BootScanPartitions     |                                                
  +----------------------------+                                                
                 |                                                              
                 |                                                              
                 |                                                              
                 |                                                              
                 v                                                              
  +----------------------------+                                                
  |scan card + load FS handlers|-MBR/GPT/flatable----+                          
  +----------------------------+               +------------------------+       
                 |                                   |                  |       
                 |                                   |                  |       
           RDB bootable                              |                  |       
                 |                                   |                  |       
                 v                                   v                  v       
  +----------------------------+               +----------+     +--------------+
  |        AddBootNode         |               |AddDosNode|     |published only|
  +----------------------------+               +----------+     +--------------+
                 |                                   |                  |       
                 |                                   |                  |       
                 |                                   |                  |       
                 |                                   |                  |       
                 v                                   |                  |       
  +----------------------------+                     |                  |       
  |     partition.resource     |<--------------------+------------------+       
  +----------------------------+                                                
@{fg text}

@{b}Hotplug attach (DOS time).@{ub} A card insert wakes the consumer's mount
worker, which publishes then mounts the card's partitions.

@{fg highlight}
  +--------------------+
  |    card insert     |
  +--------------------+
             |          
             |          
             |          
             |          
             v          
  +--------------------+
  |  mount-agent task  |
  +--------------------+
             |          
             |          
             |          
             |          
             v          
  +--------------------+
  |mount-worker process|
  +--------------------+
             |          
             |          
             |          
             |          
             v          
  +--------------------+
  |   ScanPartitions   |
  +--------------------+
             |          
             |          
             |          
             |          
             v          
  +--------------------+
  |  MountPartitions   |
  +--------------------+
             |          
             |          
             |          
             |          
             v          
  +--------------------+
  | partition.resource |
  +--------------------+
@{fg text}

@{b}Hotplug detach (card removed).@{ub} Two policies (see @{"Configuration" link configuration} ): keep the handler or
tear it down.

@{fg highlight}
  +-------------------------------+                                                                                   
  |          card remove          |                                                                                   
  +-------------------------------+                                                                                   
                  |                                                                                                   
                  |                                                                                                   
                  |                                                                                                   
                  |                                                                                                   
                  v                                                                                                   
  +-------------------------------+                                                                                   
  |      mount-worker process     |--------UNMOUNT-list-set---------+                                                 
  +-------------------------------+                                 |                                                 
                  |                                                 |                                                 
                  |                                                 |                                                 
         UNMOUNT list empty                                         |                                                 
                  |                                                 |                                                 
                  v                                                 v                                                 
  +-------------------------------+                  +----------------------------+                                   
  |           MarkAbsent          |                  |UnmountPartitions prefixList|--------------------+              
  +-------------------------------+                  +----------------------------+                    |              
                  |                                                 |                                  |              
                  |                                                 |                                  |              
                  |                                                 |                                  |              
                  |                                                 |                                  |              
                  v                                                 v                                  v              
  +-------------------------------+                  +----------------------------+     +----------------------------+
  |every entry kept, marked absent|                  |listed filesystems torn down|     |the rest kept, marked absent|
  +-------------------------------+                  +----------------------------+     +----------------------------+
@{fg text}

@{b}Handler mount, auto-detect (e.g. fat95).@{ub} A handler probes a card, lets
@{fg shine}ScanPartitions@{fg text} publish the candidates, picks its partition, and overlays
its real DOS name with @{fg shine}RegisterPartition@{fg text} .

@{fg highlight}
  +---------------------------------------+
  |               mount MS:               |
  +---------------------------------------+
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      v                    
  +---------------------------------------+
  |             fat95 handler             |
  +---------------------------------------+
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      v                    
  +---------------------------------------+
  |             ScanPartitions            |
  +---------------------------------------+
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      v                    
  +---------------------------------------+
  |          select FAT partition         |
  +---------------------------------------+
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      v                    
  +---------------------------------------+
  |           RegisterPartition           |
  +---------------------------------------+
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      |                    
                      v                    
  +---------------------------------------+
  |partition.resource: real name + MOUNTED|
  +---------------------------------------+
@{fg text}

